  "result": "The O4 quiz and its key are written. The quiz is `quizzes/0002.json`, with its key at `keys/0002.json`.\n\n- **Length:** you asked for six questions, but the quiz has ten, because you prefer ten, half definitions and half application.\n- **Order:** q1 to q5 are definition questions: workflow, agent, control flow, the trade-off an agent makes against a fixed workflow, and the model's job inside a workflow. q6 to q10 apply them to the makerspace assistant.\n- **Application items:** these cover classifying the booking flow, picking a design for an open-ended troubleshooting question, and choosing a design under the sponsor's budget. q9 is a numeric semester-cost item and q10 is a short answer on step limits.\n- **Ahead of the lessons:** no lesson covers O4 yet. I built the quiz from Anthropic's \"Building effective agents\" article, so it is ahead of the lessons. `NOTES.md` says Riley hasn't met workflows versus agents, so expect this to be a cold test.\n- **Review:** the `quiz-reviewer` subagent checked the draft, and two review-and-revise passes ran. I checked the last revision myself because no reviewer saw it. The record is in `review-records/0002-quiz.md`.\n\nThe new misconception ids M7, M9, M10 and M11 are defined only by how the key uses them, since the workspace had no definitions. The record lists their meanings.\n\nThe quiz is ready when you are.",
